   copies out, so an update writes the entry in place instead of going through
   `set`. One emitted function for both families: what differs is the declared
   return, exactly as ListRef.get (a view) and ListVal.get (a copy) already
   differ while sharing one getMut.

   Its own file, for the reason z_IdMapIter.c.tmpl is separate: a mono whose
   `getMut` never resolved must still emit its container, and a template read
   by a seed that cannot fill its holes writes them into the C verbatim. */

